/**
 * AICommandCenter.tsx
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------
 * Drop-in React/TSX version of the AI Command Center dashboard.
 * 100% faithful to the HTML/CSS build — same pixel-art scene,
 * same 13 agents, same event engine (focus/zoom, chat routing,
 * voice input + model selector, celebration banner, responsive
 * drawers). Nothing was redesigned; this is a straight port.
 *
 * WHERE TO PUT IT
 *   - Next.js (App Router):  app/dashboard/AICommandCenter.tsx
 *     Already declared as a client component ("use client").
 *   - Vite / CRA / Remix:    src/components/AICommandCenter.tsx
 *
 * DEPS
 *   Only React 18+. No CSS framework, no icon lib, no build plugins.
 *   All pixel-art assets are inlined as base64, so this file is large
 *   (~600 KB). To lazy-load, split SCENE_HTML into a separate module
 *   and dynamic-import() it.
 *
 * BACKEND HOOKS (grep these tags — this port is wired for real, not the demo loop)
 *   [BACKEND-EVENTS]  window.engine.startWork / completeWork / incident / setState — called
 *                     from the polling loop in the default export below, driven by
 *                     GET /api/dashboard/live (jobs_log + content_items). No random/demo
 *                     loop runs anymore; every animation traces back to a real DB row.
 *   [BACKEND-CHAT]    routeChat() delegates unmatched messages to window.__aicRealChat,
 *                     which streams a real POST /api/chat reply into the bubble.
 *   [BACKEND-VOICE]   startVoice() — swap the Web Speech fallback for your
 *                     STT provider; voice model dropdown is #vmodel.
 *
 * DESIGN RULES (preserved from the HTML version — DO NOT BREAK)
 *   R1 No random loops. Every motion is state-driven.
 *   R2 Idle scene = static. Bob / typing / aura only run while working / speaking.
 *   R3 Hover on cabin: cursor only, no border. Click = camera zoom + panel.
 *   R4 Camera transition: 1.15s cubic-bezier(.5,0,.15,1). Matches reference.
 *   R5 Responsive: 3 breakpoints
 *      (>=1280 three-col  ·  900-1279 chat becomes drawer  ·  <=900 both drawers).
 *
 * PROMPT FOR AI TOOLS extending this file:
 *   "Add a new agent" → append to the AGENTS array in the engine block, add
 *   its cabin markup to SCENE_HTML (see the .hs.a-<id> pattern), and add its
 *   dot/monitor coordinates. Preserve R1–R5.
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------
 */
